commit ccdc386eb0a8871b8e7e3d3d13caba593e11bb36
Author: GoodOlClint <goodolclint@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jun 29 12:26:02 2026 -0500

    Add Mixtral (sparse MoE) model (#378)
    
    Port of mlx-lm's mixtral.py: Mistral-style attention (GQA, RoPE, no
    bias) with a sparse MoE block — gate (no bias) → top-k → softmax over
    the selected expert logits → SwitchGLU. Mirrors the in-tree PhiMoE
    structure; differs in using RMSNorm (not LayerNorm), plain RoPE (not
    SuScaled), bias-free projections, and optional tied embeddings.
    
    sanitize() stacks per-expert w1/w2/w3 (weight/scales/biases) into
    switch_mlp.gate_proj/down_proj/up_proj, so both full-precision and
    pre-quantized Mixtral checkpoints load. Registered as "mixtral".
    
    Tests (MixtralTests): forward-pass logits shape on a synthetic 1-layer
    config, and sanitize() expert-stacking shape/key remap.
    
    Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

